{"id": "EUVD-2026-94402", "enisaUuid": "3f79f6fe-38a0-369b-b409-3e688ad3d8f2", "description": "Gophish through 0.12.1 contains a rate limit bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to evade /login throttling by spoofing X-Forwarded-For or X-Real-IP headers. Attackers can send a different forwarded address per request so the limiter keyed on rewritten RemoteAddr never triggers, enabling unlimited password guessing and credential stuffing.", "datePublished": "2026-10-07T15:44:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T22:06:20", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://blog.ostorlab.co/gophish-0121-manual-review-agentic-deep-scan.html", "https://github.com/gophish/gophish/blob/b1648f0759c6d57ac989157c55d8b47c40254fe6/controllers/route.go#L168", "https://github.com/gophish/gophish/blob/b1648f0759c6d57ac989157c55d8b47c40254fe6/middleware/ratelimit/ratelimit.go#L132-L136", "https://github.com/gophish/gophish", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gophish-through-0.12.1-login-rate-limit-bypass-via-x-forwarded-for-spoofing"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107271", "GHSA-hxwc-4ggw-27w5"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4cc9c901-ec1c-34d9-b457-36f567aa1f6f", "product": {"name": "gophish", "vendor": {"name": "Gophish"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.12.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9bd48317-b8da-33c8-95be-4cac1ad74147", "vendor": {"name": "Gophish"}}], "isExploited": false}